---
title: Extra Crispy Parmesan Crusted Roasted Potatoes
description: Parboiled russet potatoes tossed with butter and Parmesan into a starchy slurry, then roasted until they develop a shatteringly crisp cheese crust over a fluffy interior.
course: side
cuisine: American
servings: 6
time required: 1 hour
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 45 minutes
source: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1020633-extra-crispy-parmesan-crusted-roasted-potatoes?smid=yt-nytfood&smtyp=cur
image: https://static01.nyt.com/images/2019/11/20/dining/18Kenjirex/18Kenjirex-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg
tags:
  - potatoes
  - roasted
  - parmesan
  - crispy
  - side dish
---

Adjust the #oven{} rack to the center position and heat the oven to 425F (or 400F with convection). Line a #sheet pan{} with parchment paper.

Combine @russet potatoes{3%lbs}(peeled and cut into 1 1/2- to 2-inch chunks), @baking soda{1/2%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tbsp}, @bay leaves{4}, @black peppercorns{1%tbsp} and @garlic{3%cloves}(roughly crushed) in a large #pot{}. Cover with cold water by about an inch and bring to a boil over high heat.

Reduce to a simmer and cook until the potatoes are tender all the way to the center, about ~stovetop{10%minutes}. Drain well, discarding the bay leaves and peppercorns, and return the potatoes to the pot.

Add @unsalted butter{4%tbsp}(melted) and @grated parmesan cheese{2%oz}(about 1 cup) to the hot potatoes. Toss and fold with a rubber spatula until the Parmesan, butter and starch form a slurry over the surface of the potatoes, about 30 seconds.

Transfer the potatoes to the prepared #sheet pan{} and spread them out so they are mostly separated from one another. Roast until pale golden brown and sizzling on the bottom, about ~oven{20%minutes}.

Flip the potatoes using a thin metal spatula and continue roasting until crisp and deep gold on most sides, about ~oven{15%minutes} longer. Watch carefully toward the end and do not let them brown beyond a deep gold, or the Parmesan will turn bitter.

Remove from the oven and let cool for ~rest{5%minutes} on the pan. Transfer to a serving platter, season with @salt to taste and serve.
